{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And it was evil in his eyes</b> — Perhaps Joseph loved Manasseh more because he was the firstborn; therefore it displeased him. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that he thought his father had erred concerning them, and if his blessing had been given without awareness, his blessing would not come upon them, for it would not be in the holy spirit as fitting. And when he said to him, \"I know, my son, I know,\" he was reassured."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:30.827167993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}